Consolidated corrected copy of Sergey Senozhatsky's [PATCH v5 00/13] 'zram: redesign
zcomp and rework backends' (upstream series:
https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261018035125.3120704-1-senozhatsky@chromium.org).

Changes vs the previous hand-assembled copy (v2, 11 patches):
 1. Commits are in UPSTREAM ORDER (01..13).  The previous copy ran them as
    01,02,03,07,08,09,10,11,04,05,06, which broke patch 09's backend_lz4.c hunk #1
    (its context line is 'vfree(dict_stream);', produced by patch 05).
 2. Patches 04, 05 and 06 are the upstream text with only the LZ4 workspace
    idiom adapted to this tree, whose <linux/lz4.h> (rewritten by the stack entry
    v1_20260925_..._lib_lz4_stop_forking_upstream_lz4_vendor_it.patch) hides the
    LZ4 state layout: LZ4_stream_t / LZ4_streamHC_t / LZ4_streamDecode_t are
    incomplete union types, so upstream's 'sizeof(*x)', 'kzalloc_obj(*x)' and
    'BUILD_BUG_ON(sizeof(...))' cannot compile here; the equivalent
    LZ4_MEM_COMPRESS(16416) / LZ4HC_MEM_COMPRESS(262200) / LZ4_MEM_DECOMPRESS(32)
    constants are used instead (sizes asserted by static_assert() in
    lib/lz4/lz4_compress.c and lib/lz4/lz4hc_compress.c).  v5 carries 04..06
    byte-identically to v2, so the adaptation still stands unchanged.
 3. Patches 01,02,03 and 07,08,09 are the upstream v5 text verbatim.
 4. v5 drops v2's 10 ("use a singleton compression context...") and 11 ("use
    rw_semaphore for decompression streams") in favour of four patches: 10 shared
    decompression streams, 11 bounce buffer for spanning objects, 12 borrowing of
    idle decompression streams, and 13 the singleton compression context
    (revised).  Those four are the upstream v5 text verbatim and touch only
    zcomp.c, zcomp.h and zram_drv.c, so they do not interact with the LZ4
    adaptation.

